start launches the daemon and prints its pid (process id). With a LaunchAgent
installed it asks launchd; otherwise it spawns leylined in the background
with its output in the log file. Already running is not an error.

Usage:
  ley daemon start [flags]

Examples:
  ley daemon start         # started leylined (pid 12345); check with: ley daemon status
  ley daemon start --log /tmp/leylined.log

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for start

Global Flags:
      --bin string      path to the leylined binary
      --json            machine output: proto3 JSON (NDJSON for streams)
      --log string      daemon log file (default: ~/Library/Logs/Leyline/leylined.log)
      --socket string   daemon socket path (default: user daemon UDS, $LEYLINE_SOCKET)
